# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile files. Everything a person writes about themselves stays local.
# The engine ships in this repo, the profile never does.
# The block below is deliberately blunt: it ignores the profile file names
# anywhere in the tree, then re-allows the two places that hold engine-owned
# copies (the empty template, and the fictional example persona).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
profile.md
voice.md
pillars.md
ideas.md
measure.md
linkedin-page.md
corpus/
posts/
drafts/
interviews/

# French instance names, for anyone running a pre-migration profile
profil.md
voix.md
piliers.md
idees.md
mesure.md

# Engine-owned files that share those names, kept in the repo.
# references/ is engine-owned by definition, so nothing under it is ever
# ignored: references/measure.md was silently dropped from the first release
# by the measure.md rule above, and check.sh now fails on that class of bug.
!references/
!references/**
!examples/**

# The maintainer's own project state file, not a deliverable.
# Contributor-facing conventions live in CONTRIBUTING.md instead.
CLAUDE.md

# Same category: planning prose, in the maintainer's language, about what this
# repository will do next. The engine is English wide and a plan is not part
# of it. What a plan decided ends up in docs/journal.md, which is shipped.
plans/

# Local configuration
.env
.env.bak.*
.claude/

# Noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# app virtualenv and build leftovers
app/.venv/
app/dist/

# the macOS build: a 21 MB disk image is a release asset, not a source file
dist/
*.dmg
